.TH geectl-request-change-state 1  "geectl-request-change-state 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-change\-state \- Change a submit request\*(Aqs state to one of new/review/accepted/declined/revoked
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request change\-state\fR [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> <\fISTATE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a submit request\*(Aqs state to one of new/review/accepted/declined/revoked
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR [default: ]
The message left with the change. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a comment may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Force the change, overriding open reviews. Only honoured when changing to accepted
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The request id
.TP
<\fISTATE\fR>
The state to change to
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
new
.IP \(bu 2
review
.IP \(bu 2
accepted
.IP \(bu 2
declined
.IP \(bu 2
revoked
.RE
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
